-- title:
--   Two invariant generators on a chart near a maximal ideal
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $B$ a Noetherian commutative ring in which $p$ is nilpotent, let $X$ be a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module over $B$ — that is, a commutative two-variable formal group law $F$ over $B$ together with series-endomorphisms $\mathrm{act}(a)$ for $a$ in the Witt vectors of $\mathbb F_{p^2}$ and a series $\varpi$, all law homomorphisms of $F$, with $\mathrm{act}(1)$ the identity, $\mathrm{act}$ multiplicative and additive via $F$, $\varpi\circ\varpi=\mathrm{act}(p)$ and $\varpi\circ\mathrm{act}(a)=\mathrm{act}(\varphi a)\circ\varpi$ — let $I\subseteq B[\![x_0,x_1]\!]$ be an ideal and $h$ a natural number. Assume: $B[\![x]\!]/I$ is a finite projective $B$-module; for every field $\kappa$ and every ring homomorphism $f\colon B\to\kappa$ the quotient $\kappa[\![x]\!]/I\kappa[\![x]\!]$ has $\kappa$-dimension $p^h$; some power $x_i^q$ lies in $I$ for both $i$; every element of $I$ has zero constant coefficient; for $f\in I$ the series $f(F(y,z))$ lies in the ideal of $B[\![y,z]\!]$ generated by $I(y)\cup I(z)$; and $I$ is stable under substitution of $\mathrm{act}(a)$ for every $a$ and of $\varpi$. Let $\mathfrak m\subset B$ be maximal. Then there is $s\in B\setminus\mathfrak m$ such that, writing $B_s$ for the localisation away from $s$ and $I_s$ for the image of $I$ in $B_s[\![x_0,x_1]\!]$, the quotient $B_s[\![x]\!]/I_s$ is a finite free $B_s$-module, some power $x_{i}^{q}$ lies in $I_s$ for both $i$, and there are two series $u_0,u_1\in B_s[\![x_0,x_1]\!]$ with zero constant coefficients such that $u_j(F(y,z))-u_j(y)$ lies in the ideal generated by $I_s(z)$, where $F$ is the base change of $X$'s group law to $B_s$, and such that $u_0,u_1$ generate $I_s$.
--
--   This is the local form, at a single maximal ideal of the base, of the statement that the ideal of an $\mathcal O_D$-stable finite locally free infinitesimal subgroup of a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module becomes, on a basic open chart, generated by two primitive (group-like) series with free quotient. It is the input to [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_cover_free_and_span_range_eq_map_of_subgroup_ideal`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_cover_free_and_span_range_eq_map_of_subgroup_ideal), which glues such charts over a finite cover of $\operatorname{Spec} B$.
